<TD> <FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif"> <B>MoKB Recruiting Committee</B><BR>Please contact these people in game or via PM (links provided) with any recruiting questions.  The Recruiting Commitee and your sponsor work together to keep you informed and interested in MoKB during your recruiting period.<BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000010" TARGET=_blank>Alerik</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000016" TARGET=_blank>Denuvien</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000015" TARGET=_blank>Frehya</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000012" TARGET=_blank>Lannear</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000035" TARGET=_blank>Nimowei</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000023" TARGET=_blank>Ortin</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000039" TARGET=_blank>Syrith</A><P><BR><B>MoKB Officer List</B><BR>Officer List with PM Links:<BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000004" TARGET=_blank>Gnosh - Diplomat</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000019" TARGET=_blank>Timarak - HR</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000002" TARGET=_blank>Malik(Shoon) - Web Master</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000005" TARGET=_blank>Frax - Raid Planner</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000009" TARGET=_blank>Aelori - Raid Planner</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/UBB/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000016" TARGET=_blank>Denuvien - Recruiting</A><P><B>MoKB Recruiting</B><P>Update - 2/14/02<BR><I>MoKB has been growing fast in the last couple months. At the current time, we would like to slow down our active recruiting as the guild learns its new strengths and weaknesses. Class balance and level range are critical to a guild for both experience groups and raids. Currently, we feel that our recruits should be at least level 58 to mesh well with our guild - our average level is currently 59.5. The classes we have the most need for are druids, shaman, necros, and bards. Both of these criteria are loose as we are a very friendly guild but the tradeoff between guildsize, balance, and the ability to do the raids desired by the members is very tricky. Please don't read this and become discouraged -- read it and become motivated to work to fit in, to meet people, and to make your mark on MoKB by proving that you can help our guild become stronger.<P>The best way to express interest in MoKB is to talk to and meet our members, especially our Recruiting Commitee, in game. Hopefully you will develop a close rapport with one who will be willing to step up and sponsor you. If you are having a hard time finding a sponor, please use the links above to Private Message the members of our Recruiting Committee or talk to them in game.</I><P><BR>A) Express Interest and get involved. The BEST way to do this is to contact our Recruiting Committee via PM or in game.  Public notices on the BBoard had a bad habit of getting lost so until we get a recruiting form, please contact the Recruiting Committee.<P>B) YOU need to find a SPONSOR. A sponsor is a current MoKB member that is willing to take you under his or her wing and explain what's going on and help you get to know the rest of MoKB. Ideally your sponsor should be someone you have known for some time (and preferably has been in MoKB for a while) although neither is required. It is VERY important to realize that our recruit process is NOT FAST, it can take a month or more to go from a recruit to a member. The more you show up for raids and get to know people, the faster this time will go (And the more fun you will have as a recruit). If you feel like you've been forgotten or are being dragged along bug your sponsor or a member of the Recruiting Commitee.<P>C) Once you have a sponsor you will become an official recruit and given access to the "Cub Corner" and "Events" forums. First you should post a nice long post in Cub Corner about why you would make a good Kaer Baar. Then you should check Events as often as possible to see what official preplanned events you can get involved in. You should also check with your sponsor as often as possible to see if there are any unofficial raids or groups that you can join.<P>F) Your SPONSOR will begin a thread in our recruit forum listing your qualifications and raids attended. You may want to work with your sponsor to make sure this is as accurate as possible, as this thread is intended to give the guild as a whole an idea of how your time as a recruit is being spent.<P>G) After a couple weeks a vote is taken among the members. This vote can have three results, listed from worst to best. <BR>No: Sorry, you're not fit for MoKB for one reason or another. <BR>Wait: Not enough members know you or feel comfortable with you quite yet and would like a little longer to get to know you (in which case you remain a recruit and we automatically take another vote a week later). <BR>Yes: You're given temporory access to /gu. After one week in /gu we take another vote for final membership approval, which can have the same results except for a "Yes" grants you full guild membership.<P>It can be a little confusing, but three main points are:<P>1) You need to be pro-active and make sure you get on raids and in groups and make a friend (if you dont' have one already) that can be your sponsor and guide you through the process.<BR>2) Our process can be slow, but it's designed to make sure that MoKB is the both capable of killing the things we want to kill and capable of having a good time doing it. If you feel like it's dragging out, talk to your sponsor to make sure things are moving along as quickly as they should be.<BR>3) Your time as a guest and a recruit should be fun, and it's our desire that it's as exciting and full of adventure as it can be.<P>[ February 14, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<P>[ February 14, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<P>[ April 06, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<P>[ April 06, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<P>[ May 15, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<P>[ May 15, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<P>[ May 15, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<P>[ May 15, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<p>[ June 27, 2002: Message edited by: Gnosh Gneurotic ]<P>--------------------<P><B><A HREF="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=88890" TARGET=_blank>Gnosh Gneurotic</A></B><BR><I>did you hear the distant cry -- calling me back to my sin </I> 
</FONT> 
